original:
The man that was drowned. A sail veering about the blank bay waiting
for a swollen bundle to bob up, roll over to the sun a puffy face,
saltwhite. Here I am.

after:
_—Græd ikke mere, sorgfulde hyrder, græd ikke mere,
for Lycidas, som I sørger over, er ikke død,
om han end sank under vandets gulv ..._
